The amount of such dividends will be determined by our board of directors and
will depend on the amount of our available cash flow, current and projected cash
requirements, tax considerations and other factors.



     As of the date of this prospectus, we have no real estate investments. We
will use the first $25,000,000 we raise in this offering, plus an additional
$10,000,000 an affiliate of Hines will contribute to the Operating Partnership
when the minimum offering is reached, to acquire an interest in the Core Fund.
We may receive quarterly dividends from the Core Fund, which may allow us to pay
dividends to our shareholders. Other than this initial interest in the Core
Fund, we do not expect to make additional investments in real estate investments
until we identify investment opportunities and raise sufficient capital pursuant
to this offering to do so. We cannot predict when, if ever, we will begin to
generate sufficient cash flow from these additional investments to pay dividends
