satisfy the distribution requirements for a taxable year, we would be
disqualified as a REIT, unless we were permitted to pay a deficiency
distribution to our shareholders, as well as any required interest thereon to
the IRS. A deficiency distribution cannot be used to satisfy the distribution
requirement, however, if the failure to meet the requirement is not due to a
later adjustment to our income by the IRS.

